.env

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Generated release data. Everything here is published to Hugging Face under
# releases/, so committing it duplicated ~379 MB into the repository for no gain.
# The per-day metrics that only ever existed here are preserved in
# archive/daily-metrics/.
output/
latest/
data/brrrdle/

# Large data files (stored on Hugging Face, not in git)
initial_deliverables/
initial_deliverables.zip
*.json
!templates/*.json
!overall_stats.json
# The archived per-day metrics are the only surviving copy of these files, so
# they must survive the blanket *.json rule above. This negation works because
# archive/ is not itself excluded -- git will not re-include a file whose parent
# directory is ignored.
!archive/**/*.json
# Which words have already been checked against the dictionary APIs, and the one
# thing carrying that knowledge between runs. Without it every run starts from
# "Already validated: 0" and re-samples the same 9.27 million words, spending API
# quota on entries that were already settled. The blanket *.json above was
# catching it, and nothing noticed because validation produced no output for 199
# days -- the file was never written, so the rule was never exercised.
!validation_progress.json

# --- Website -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Two things above fight a JavaScript workspace, and both fail silently.
#
# The blanket `*.json` swallows package.json, every tsconfig, and the web app
# manifest. It is the same rule that broke the 2026-08-12 daily run, and the
# daily workflow now hard-errors on a produced-but-ignored path rather than
# skipping it, so anything missed here surfaces as a red build rather than a
# quiet omission.
#
# The Python template's generic directory names -- `lib/`, `build/`, `dist/`,
# `downloads/` -- match ordinary source paths anywhere in the tree, not just at
# the root. `site/src/lib/` would have been ignored wholesale. The source tree
# uses `util/` instead of `lib/` so that trap cannot be re-sprung by a later
# rename, and the rest are re-included by name below.
!package.json
!tsconfig*.json
!site/package.json
!site/tsconfig*.json
!site/src/**/*.json
!site/public/**/*.json
!tools/eol-build/package.json
!tools/eol-build/tsconfig*.json
# How to start the dev server. Worth committing: it is the answer to "how do I
# run this", and the blanket *.json above would otherwise hide it.
!.claude/launch.json

# Generated on every build by tools/eol-build, from Hugging Face. Committing it
# would put a fresh ~700 KB of binary in git history daily for no gain -- the
# deploy rebuilds it from the live dataset anyway. Listed after the negations
# above because the last matching rule wins.
site/public/data/
site/public/downloads/
# Regenerated from _posts/ on every build. Committing them would put a new
# feed.xml in history every morning for no gain.
site/public/feed.xml
site/public/sitemap.xml
site/public/robots.txt
node_modules/
.cache/

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# pytest
.pytest_cache/

# Phase 1 evidence layer — derived data is reproducible from the manifest;
# adjudication logs are personal working data bound for the private archive
research/data/
research/adjudicate/logs/
research/adjudicate/decks/
# The per-source frame-contribution summary is a RESULT the SR2 report cites,
# a few hundred bytes — it survives the blanket *.json like the others above.
!research/frame_contributions.json
!research/features_manifest.json
!research/productivity_table.json
!research/phase2_gate.json
